                <pb facs="0463" n="319" xml:id="pg319"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77 Chinese Eastern/328: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-09-13T17:00:00+08:00">September 13, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 14—12:10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>825. My 772, August 31, 1 p.m. Following from American Consul at Harbin: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“September 12, 11 a.m. Vice Consul Lilliestrom visited concentration camp
                            for student civilian prisoners September 10th, total prisoners 1170, 70
                            women and 13 children under five years. Prisoners crowded in dark, damp
                            quarters, sanitary conditions bad, food sufficient but of poor quality,
                            drinking water from the river, stomach trouble prevalent and epidemic
                            feared, medical attention and exercise facilities inadequate.
                            Communication with relatives provided for, no discretion allowed, only
                            occasional complaints of intentional maltreatment by Chinese who promise
                            improvement sanitary conditions but are very dilatory.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
